# Copy to .env and fill in. Nothing in this repository auto-loads a .env: export
# it yourself, or hand these to the server through your MCP client's `env` block
# or `docker run --env-file`.
#
# These four are what you need to start. The optional knobs — MAX_ORDER_NOTIONAL_USD,
# TASTYTRADE_READ_ONLY, TASTYTRADE_HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS, TASTYTRADE_MAX_RESPONSE_BYTES,
# TASTYTRADE_HTTP_WALL_CLOCK_MS, TASTYTRADE_ACCEPT_VERSION,
# TASTYTRADE_USER_AGENT, TASTYTRADE_ALLOW_UNKNOWN_API_HOST,
# TASTYTRADE_CREDENTIAL_CHANNEL, TASTYTRADE_ALLOW_PROXY — are documented in the
# README's Configuration table.
#
# TASTYTRADE_ALLOW_UNKNOWN_API_HOST is the one to know about before you need it:
# if TASTYTRADE_API_URL below names a host that is not a tastytrade API host —
# a proxy, a gateway, a local test double — the server REFUSES TO START rather
# than send the refresh token and client secret there. Name that exact hostname
# in TASTYTRADE_ALLOW_UNKNOWN_API_HOST to allow it.
#
# If your machine routes outbound HTTP through a proxy, or trusts an extra
# certificate authority, this server says so on stderr and keeps going. Set
# TASTYTRADE_CREDENTIAL_CHANNEL=strict to make that a refusal instead, and name
# your own gateway's hostname in TASTYTRADE_ALLOW_PROXY to permit it.
#
# The API URL below is the SANDBOX. Point it at https://api.tastyworks.com only
# when you intend to trade real money.
TASTYTRADE_API_URL=https://api.cert.tastyworks.com
TASTYTRADE_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id
TASTYTRADE_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret
TASTYTRADE_REFRESH_TOKEN=your_refresh_token
